WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.970
Are people becoming addicted to technology?
人们正在对科技上瘾吗？

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:12.180
Some researchers warn that heavy use of technology can affect the brain much as drugs do.
一些研究者警告说，过度使用科技对大脑的影响和毒品很相似。

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:20.080
When we look around, it is hard to disagree: many people today are indeed becoming addicted to technology.
环顾四周，我们很难不同意：如今许多人确实正在对科技上瘾。

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.850
Signs of this addiction are everywhere.
这种上瘾的迹象随处可见。

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.330
On the subway, almost everyone is staring at a phone screen.
地铁上，几乎人人都盯着手机屏幕。

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.550
At dinner, friends check their messages instead of talking to each other.
吃饭时，朋友们各自看手机消息，而不是互相交谈。

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:39.520
Many students scroll through short videos late into the night and feel anxious whenever their phones are out of reach.
许多学生刷短视频一直刷到深夜，手机一不在身边就感到焦虑。

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:49.400
One reason for this is that apps are designed to keep users hooked with endless updates, likes and notifications, which give people constant small rewards.
原因之一是，应用程序的设计就是用没完没了的更新、点赞和通知让用户欲罢不能，这些不断给人带来小小的奖赏。

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.300
However, technology is not the enemy; the real problem is our lack of self-control.
然而，科技并不是敌人；真正的问题在于我们缺乏自制力。

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:10.570
To avoid becoming slaves to technology, we should set limits on our screen time, turn off unnecessary notifications and spend more time on real-world activities such as reading, sports and face-to-face conversations with family and friends.
为了避免沦为科技的奴隶，我们应该限制屏幕使用时间，关闭不必要的通知，并多花时间参加现实生活中的活动，比如阅读、运动以及与家人朋友面对面交谈。

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.910
Only when we stay in control can technology truly serve us.
只有我们保持掌控，科技才能真正为我们服务。
